This master specification upgrades the initial DE RIDE v1.0 draft into an enterprise-grade, production-ready architecture tailored for Ogun State and Lagos with national scalability, incorporating your exact business rules, Groq-powered Amebo AI, multi-tier subscriptions, rank/medal gamification, and end-to-end technical blueprints.
1. Brand Identity, Color System & UI/UX Architecture
Selected Color Palette: Logo-Matched Modern (High Contrast & Sleek)
Looking directly at your official DE RIDE brand mark (1794927085562.jpg), the Logo-Matched Modern palette is the unequivocal winner. It creates immediate visual continuity between the emblem and the UI while delivering OLED battery savings for drivers/passengers on long trips and razor-sharp contrast in bright outdoor motor parks.
 * Primary Background (Canvas): Deep Charcoal/Slate #1B2428
 * Elevated Surface / Cards / Bottom Sheets: Dark Gunmetal #243036 (1px border #324149)
 * Primary Navigation / Active Routes / Trust Accents: Ocean Teal #1A7D82 (Hover/Active: #229EA4)
 * Primary CTAs / Destination Pins / Alerts: Vibrant Coral #F46A6A (Hover/Active: #FF7E7E)
 * Primary Typography: Crisp Pure White #FFFFFF
 * Secondary Typography / Metadata: Cool Mist #9FB1B9
 * Success / Verified Badge / Online Status: Emerald Mint #10B981
 * Warning / Cooldown Timer / Grace Period: Solar Amber #F59E0B
UI/UX & App Layout Architecture (Low-Literacy & High-Speed Optimized)
 * App Shell & Navigation:
   * Persistent Top Header (56px): DE RIDE SVG Logo (left), Language & Voice Toggle (EN | YO | HA | IG | PCM with Web Speech API audio read-aloud icon), and Amebo AI Token Pill (e.g., ⚡ 10 Tokens).
   * Interactive Map Canvas (65% Viewport Height on Home): Custom dark-mode Google Maps (#1B2428 base geometry, #1A7D82 highway strokes, #F46A6A custom SVG park/destination pins).
   * Draggable Bottom Sheet (35%–85% Viewport Height): Snap-to-grid cards with minimum 48px × 48px touch targets, high-contrast progress bars for seat capacity (11/14 Seats), and visual iconography next to every label.
   * Bottom Navigation Bar (64px, 5 Tabs): Explore Parks | My Tickets (QR) | Bike Hail | Amebo AI | Profile & Rank.
2. Upgraded Core Business Logic & Operational Rules
2.1 Launch Geography & Scalability
 * Phase 1 Active Geofence: Ogun State & Lagos State (e.g., Berger, Ojota, Oshodi, Jibowu, Maza-Maza, Abeokuta Kuto/Itoku, Sagamu Interchange, Ijebu-Ode, Sango-Ota).
 * Architecture Readiness: Database schemas and Google Maps geofencing polygons are built multi-state ready (state_code indexing) so expanding nationwide requires zero schema migrations—only toggling is_active = TRUE on new state/park records.
2.2 Park Visibility, Multi-Source GPS & 120-Second Cooldown Lock
 * Dual Visibility Mode:
   * Manual Park Queue Mode: Park Operators, Dispatchers, and Drivers manually log bus arrival, seat count, and scheduled departure.
   * Live GPS Telemetry Mode (Opt-In): Users explicitly opt in to background/foreground telemetry (acknowledging data/battery responsibility). GPS coordinates stream every 10 seconds via WebSockets from three prioritized sources:
     * Priority 1: Dedicated Vehicle OBD/GPS Hardware (if installed).
     * Priority 2: Driver App (navigator.geolocation high-accuracy stream).
     * Priority 3: Dispatcher App (while bus is stationary inside park geofence).
 * 120-Second Capacity & Departure Lock (Anti-Manipulation Engine):
   * Whenever a Park Operator, Driver, or Dispatcher updates available_seats or estimated_departure_time, the server writes a Redis/In-Memory lock key trip_lock:{trip_id} with a 120-second TTL and stores last_status_updated_at in PostgreSQL.
   * Any subsequent update attempt within 120 seconds returns HTTP 429 Too Many Requests with retry_after_seconds (e.g., "Locked for 84s to prevent passenger confusion"). UI displays a live countdown ring.
2.3 Financial Engine, Fees & Refund/Cancellation Matrix
 * Checkout Breakdown (Passenger Pays All Fees Transparently):
   
   * Paystack Fee Formula (Nigeria): 1.5\% \text{ of subtotal} + ₦100 (waived for transactions under ₦2,500, capped at ₦2,000), passed explicitly as paystack_fee line item.
 * Strict Refund & Cancellation Logic:
   * Non-Refundable Components: The ₦20 DE RIDE fee and the Paystack Processing Fee are NEVER refunded under any circumstance. All percentages below apply strictly to the Base Ticket Fare.
   * Refund Destination: User chooses at cancellation/claim time between Instant DE RIDE Wallet Credit (0 fee, immediate) or Original Funding Bank Account via Paystack Transfer API (settles within T+1).
| Scenario | Trigger Condition | Base Fare Refund % | DE RIDE ₦20 Fee | Paystack Fee |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Passenger Cancellation | Passenger cancels before bus departs | 100% Refund | Non-Refundable | Non-Refundable |
| Late Arrival | Passenger arrives/scans > 10 minutes after scheduled/agreed departure time (bus already departed or missed window) | 80% Refund | Non-Refundable | Non-Refundable |
| No-Show | Trip departs/completes with zero scan and zero prior cancellation | 40% Refund | Non-Refundable | Non-Refundable |
| Operator/Driver Cancellation | Bus trip cancelled by Park/Driver | 100% Refund (+ ₦20 waived/credited) | Credited | Non-Refundable |
2.4 Real-Time Ephemeral Chat & Immediate Escalation Pipeline
 * Trip Chat Lifecycle: Automatically created when a trip opens for boarding (status = BOARDING). Accessible to paid ticket holders, the assigned Driver, and the Park Dispatcher.
 * 6-Minute Ephemeral Purge Rule: When the trip status changes to ARRIVED / COMPLETED, a scheduled BullMQ/Node cron worker triggers at completed_at + 6 minutes to hard-delete all rows in messages for that trip_id and purge Cloudinary voice/image attachments—unless an active Dispute/Report flag is attached to the trip (which freezes the chat log into dispute_evidence_archive).
 * Real-Time Admin Escalation Path:
   * User taps Emergency / Report Issue inside Trip Chat or Active Ride screen.
   * WebSocket emits escalation:trigger immediately to the DE RIDE Live Admin Command Center with GPS coordinates, trip manifest, and last 20 messages.
   * Admin joins the live room within seconds (role: 'admin_mediator'), locking funds in escrow and bridging communication directly between User \leftrightarrow DE RIDE Admin \leftrightarrow Driver / Dispatcher / Biker in real time.
3. Tiered Subscription Ecosystem (Passengers, Drivers, Dispatchers & Operators)
All users can start on a base tier and upgrade seamlessly at any time. Rule Enforcement: The ₦60,000 One-Time Lifetime Plan is strictly restricted to Passengers (role === 'passenger'); Drivers, Dispatchers, and Park Operators are blocked at API and UI levels from purchasing the ₦60k one-time plan and instead choose from Per-Trip/Per-Bus or Monthly tiers.
